window.__F=window.__F||{};window.__F["acc-01.html"]="<div class=\"ac-info\"><p class=\"ac-i-main\">دليل تشخيص عقل مثبّت السرعة التكيّفي ACC (الرادار الأمامي). أغلب أكواده فقدان اتصال أو بيانات غير منطقية من عقول أخرى (U)، وأعطال حساسات وESP والكاميرا (C).</p><p class=\"ac-i-tip\"><b>متى تستعمله:</b> استعمله عند ظهور رسالة عطل لمثبّت السرعة أو تحذير الاصطدام الأمامي. بعض الأكواد تطلب محاذاة الحساس أو مسح الأكواد بعد برمجة العقل.</p><div class=\"ac-chips\"><span class=\"en-chip\">B = كهرباء الجسم: 1</span><span class=\"en-chip\">C = الهيكل والحساسات: 21</span><span class=\"en-chip\">P = نقل الحركة: 2</span><span class=\"en-chip\">U = اتصال الشبكة: 29</span></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong>كيف تقرأ كود العطل</strong><small>الرقم بعد الشرطة يدل على نوع العطل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-legend\"><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-11</b><span>قصر على الأرضي</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-12</b><span>قصر على البطارية</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-13</b><span>دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-15</b><span>قصر على البطارية أو دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-16</b><span>الفولتية أقل من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-17</b><span>الفولتية أعلى من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-2A</b><span>مفتاح عالق Stuck</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-84 / 85</b><span>الإشارة أقل / أعلى من المدى</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-92</b><span>أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-00</b><span>عطل عام أو بدون نوع محدد</span></div></div><p class=\"bcm-note\">الحرف الأول: B = كهرباء الجسم · C = الهيكل والحساسات · P = نقل الحركة · U = اتصال الشبكة. نفّذ دائماً الفحص المسبق Pre-Diagnostic قبل خطوات أي كود.</p></div></details></div><input type=\"search\" class=\"ec-search acc-q\" placeholder=\"ابحث: كود العطل أو كلمة من الوصف\" aria-label=\"بحث\"><p class=\"bcm-note acc-cnt\">53 كود عطل. اضغط على الكود لترى شرحه.</p><div class=\"acc-list\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b222f-00 flash write performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B222F-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">FLASH WRITE PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Continuously with the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The module disables a safety controller when programming the module with new software. The safety controller stops the controller from resetting during a flash update. This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) indicates that the controller has not reset.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) and Forward Collision Warning (FCW) systems will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC and FCW features will return to normal operation.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from off to on at least five times, leaving the ignition on for a minimum of 90 seconds per cycle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">With a scan tool, program the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module with latest software version and align the ACC Module in accordance with the Service Information. After the above procedure, Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CONTINUED ACTIVE DTC AFTER PROGRAMING</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display this DTC as active after programming?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and align the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this Module. Wiggle the wiring and connectors while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check Service Bulletins for any possible causes that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c0063-9a yaw rate sensor - component or system operating conditions\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C0063-9A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">YAW RATE SENSOR - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OPERATING CONDITIONS</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">A ready conflict between the ACC Module and the Electronic Stability Program (ESP) system has occurred. The Module receives over the CAN Bus from the Antilock Brake System (ABS) Module that the yaw rate offset of the Dynamic Sensor is beyond an allowable threshold of 4 degrees per second.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) and Forward Collision Warning (FCW) systems will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC and FCW features will return to normal operation.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ANTILOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) DTCS PRESENT</li><li>ABS MODULE DYNAMIC SENSOR</li><li>ABS MODULE NOT INITIALIZED/PROGRAMED</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Test drive the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Park the vehicle on a level surface and allow to idle for a minimum of 10 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase ACC DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool read ACC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does this DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">If the DTC can be erased without returning, no further repair is necessary, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>This DTC is an informational DTC detecting that there is a DTC stored in the Anti-lock Brake System (ABS) Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">View repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the ABS DTC(s). Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            It may be necessary to perform the ABS Initialization routine with the scan tool to reset the vehicle configuration.</div></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c008e-00 ecu internal performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C008E-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ECU INTERNAL PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module runs a self diagnostic test to validate proper controller operation. This DTC will set if the controller has failed one or more internal test.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this Module. Wiggle the wiring and connectors while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check Service Bulletins for any possible causes that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c1240-00 steering angle sensor angle overtravel performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C1240-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">STEERING ANGLE SENSOR ANGLE OVERTRAVEL PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">A ready conflict with the Steering Column Control Module (SCCM) has occurred. The Module receives a message over the Can Bus from the Steering Column Control Module (SCCM) that the Steering Angle Sensor (SAS) steering angle offset is beyond an allowable threshold of 12 degrees.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>STEERING COLUMN CONTROL MODULE DTCS PRESENT</li><li>STEERING COLUMN CONTROL MODULE (SCCM) - STEERING ANGLE SENSOR</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase ACC DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Start the Engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">If the DTC can be erased without returning, no further repair is necessary, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>REPAIR STEERING COLUMN CONTROL MODULE DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>This DTC is an informational DTC indicating that there is a DTC stored in the Steering Column Control Module (SCCM).</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">View repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the SCCM DTC(s). Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c127a-00 esp did not respond to deceleration request\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C127A-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ESP DID NOT RESPOND TO DECELERATION REQUEST</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode. ACC or Forward Collision Warning (FCW) system is enabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects the Antilock Brake System (ABS) Module for ESP/ESC does not brake when requested.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ANTILOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) ESP/ESC DTCS PRESENT</li><li>CAN MESSAGE CONFLICT</li><li>VEHICLE IMPROPERLY CONFIGURED</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Test drive the vehicle.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Park the vehicle on a level surface and allow to idle for a minimum of 10 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase ACC DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Activate the ACC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool read ACC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does this DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">If the DTC can be erased without returning, no further repair is necessary, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>This DTC is an informational DTC detecting that there is a DTC stored in the Anti-lock Brake System (ABS) Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">View repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the ABS DTC(s). Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            It may be necessary to perform the ABS Initialization routine with the scan tool to reset the vehicle configuration.</div></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c14a3-00 xbw rule violation\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C14A3-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">XBW RULE VIOLATION</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode. ACC or Forward Collision Warning (FCW) system is enabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Module detects an sudden deceleration/acceleration induced externally or a DTC in another Module.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DTCS IN OTHER MODULE(S)</li><li>IGNITION CYCLE</li><li>BRAKE SYSTEM FUNCTIONALITY</li><li>DRIVING CONDITIONS OR ACCIDENT OCCURRED</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR DTCS IN OTHER MODULES</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are other modules reporting any DTCs?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">If DTCs are set in the PCM, TCM, or ABS, Refer to DTC INDEX for those diagnostic categories first and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure(s).</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          To help in the service of the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system, it is recommended to communicate with the customer to obtain the environmental conditions they were driving in when the cruise control concern took place. Heavy rain, snow, ice, and fog can cause the ACC system to become inoperative. This is considered as a normal operational</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">reaction of the ACC system and no repair is necessary.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, attempt to erase Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Can you erase this DTC?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">If the DTC can be erased without resetting, no further repair is necessary. Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This DTC cannot be caused without faults elsewhere, other than deceleration/acceleration induced externally (e.g. driving in sand or accident).</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">If there are no other DTCs present, and the DTC cannot be cleared or go into a stored state, replace and program the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c14a4-00 sensor adjustment required\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C14A4-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SENSOR ADJUSTMENT REQUIRED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects that it is physically misaligned for one minute.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) MODULE/LENS MISALIGNED</li><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) MODULE BRACKET, SECURING CLIPS BROKEN OR</li><li>BENT</li><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          A secure and unmodified mounting location is critical to the proper operation of the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          To help in the service of the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system, it is recommended to communicate with the customer to obtain the environmental conditions they were driving in when the cruise control concern took place. Heavy rain, snow, ice, and fog can cause the ACC system to become inoperative. This is considered as a normal operational reaction of the ACC system and no repair is necessary.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Vehicles that have had the suspension modified and/or an aftermarket grill installed that blocks the ACC Module can cause the ACC system to not function properly.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Make sure the lens is free of dirt, damage, and other obstructions. Clear the DTC and verify proper operation of the ACC system.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>INSPECT ACC MODULE MOUNTING AND LENS ALIGNMENT</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Make sure the ACC Sensor lens is free from dirt and debris (mud, dirt, ice, road debris) that would compromise the function of the ACC system.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform a thorough visual and physical inspect of the ACC Module and the mounting bracket and location.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for:</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Bent mounting bracket Damage to the ACC Module Damaged, obscured, or out of alignment lens ACC Module not fully seated or broken/missing securing clips</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair as necessary in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Align the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module/sensor lens in accordance to the Service Information. If the alignment is correct, and the DTC continues to set, replace and program the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c14a5-00 sensor blinded\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C14A5-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SENSOR BLINDED</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects that the lens is damaged or obstructed.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>SENSOR LENS OBSTRUCTION</li><li>DAMAGE SENSOR LENS OR MOUNTING LOCATION</li><li>VERTICAL MISALIGNMENT</li><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          A secure and unmodified mounting location is critical to the proper operation of the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          To help in the service of the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system, it is recommended to communicate with the customer to obtain the environmental conditions they were driving in when the cruise control concern took place. Heavy rain, snow, ice, and fog can cause the ACC system to become inoperative. This is considered as a normal operational reaction of the ACC system and no repair is necessary.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Vehicles that have had the suspension modified and/or an aftermarket grill installed that blocks the ACC Module can cause the ACC system to not function properly.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Wait a minimum of one minute.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Make sure the lens is free of dirt, damage, and other obstructions. If no problems are found, clear the DTC and verify proper operation of the ACC system. Test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>INSPECT ACC MODULE MOUNTING AND LENS ALIGNMENT</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Make sure the ACC Sensor lens is free from dirt and debris (mud, dirt, ice, road debris) that would compromise the function of the ACC system.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Perform a thorough visual and physical inspection of the ACC Module and the mounting bracket and location.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for:</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Bent mounting bracket Damage to the ACC Module Damaged, obscured, or out of alignment lens ACC Module not fully seated or broken/missing securing clips</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair as necessary in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Align the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module/sensor lens in accordance to the Service Information. If the alignment is correct, and the DTC continues to set, replace and program the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c14a6-92 vehicle reaction - performance or incorrect operation\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C14A6-92</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">VEHICLE REACTION - PERFORMANCE OR INCORRECT OPERATION</small><small>العطل: أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode. ACC System enabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects when a request for acceleration or deceleration, the vehicle speed is either greater, smaller, our out of a specified range then requested.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>OTHER MODULES REPORTING DTCS PRESENT</li><li>VEHICLE IMPROPERLY CONFIGURED</li><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR OTHER DTCS</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           To help in the service of the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system, it is recommended to communicate with the customer to obtain the environmental conditions they were driving in when the cruise control concern took place. Heavy rain, snow, ice, and fog can cause the ACC system to become inoperative. This is considered as a normal operational reaction of the ACC system and no repair is necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Ignition on, engine not running.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, check DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are any other module reporting DTCs?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to DTC INDEX the appropriate diagnostic procedure and repair as necessary.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">This DTC is an informational DTC. Check all supporting systems for proper operation such as engine, transmission and braking systems. A vehicle collision can also cause this DTC to set. Make sure the vehicle supporting systems are properly configured. If no other DTCs are present and no other problems are found, replace and program the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c15d8-00 mismatch tire size\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C15D8-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">MISMATCH TIRE SIZE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus DTCs present.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects that the tire size on the vehicle is greater the 10% of the programed size.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT TIRE SIZE PROGRAMED INTO BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM)</li><li>INCORRECT TIRE SIZE PROGRAMED INTO ANTILOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS)</li><li>ANTILOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) DTCS PRESENT</li><li>WRONG TIRE SIZE INSTALLED ON VEHICLE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK THE TIRE SIZE</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>This is an informational Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC). The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module receives the vehicle configuration information over the Can Bus. Tire size is stored in the Body Control Module (BCM) and also in the Anti-lock Brake System (ABS) Module.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Possible causes but not limited too:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Wrong tires installed on vehicle. Incorrect tire size written/stored in the BCM and/or ABS. ABS DTCs present. Any Service Bulletins that may apply.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Were any of the above conditions present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair/reprogram as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">With the scan tool, perform an ACC Aim Mode - Auto Alignment procedure to relearn a different tire size and to verify the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module alignment.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c15dc-2a forward collision warning control switch-stuck\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C15DC-2A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">FORWARD COLLISION WARNING CONTROL SWITCH-STUCK</small><small>العطل: عالق (Stuck)</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Continuously with the engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module has received over the Can Bus that the Forward Collision Warning Switch is stuck in an on position.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>FORWARD COLLISION WARNING SWITCH STUCK</li><li>FORWARD COLLISION WARNING SWITCH (POD SWITCH)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>READ AND RECORD DTCS AND ENVIRONMENTAL DATA - ERASE DTCS AND CHECK FOR DTC TO RETURN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs in all Electronic Control Units (ECUs) and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, run a vehicle Scan Report, or record the Environmental Data related to the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase all DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition off for a minimum of 10 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle for at least 2 minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the TESTING FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION. Refer to TESTING FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>REPLACE THE FORWARD COLLISION WARNING SWITCH - ERASE DTCS AND CHECK FOR DTC TO RETURN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Replace the Forward Collision Warning Switch in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to POD, SWITCH BANK, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase ACC DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition off for a minimum of 10 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle for at least 2 minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replacing the Forward Collision Warning Switch corrected the condition.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all ACC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect all ACC harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">the connector locks are fully engaged.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Reconnect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Reconnect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Turn the ignition off for a minimum of 10 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Start the engine and allow it to idle for at least 2 minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repairing the wiring or the connectors corrected the condition.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c2129-16 battery voltage - circuit voltage below threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C2129-16</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BATTERY VOLTAGE - CIRCUIT VOLTAGE BELOW THRESHOLD</small><small>العطل: فولتية الدائرة أقل من الحد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. Engine not cranking. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The monitored voltage to the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is below 9.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Wipe Off Front Radar Sensor plus Graphic&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RELATED DTCS PRESENT IN POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM)</li><li>LOW BATTERY VOLTAGE</li><li>FUSED IGNITION OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>RELATED DTCS PRESENT IN THE PCM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Powertrain Control Module (PCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any charging system or battery related DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the PCM DTC(s). Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the TESTING FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION. Refer to TESTING FOR AN INTERMITTENT CONDITION .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (F948) FUSED IGNITION CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the ACC Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F948) Fused Ignition circuit at the ACC Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F948) Fused Ignition circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the fuse is open, make sure to check for a short to ground.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (Z902) GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using a 12-volt test light connected to 12-volts, check the ground and the (Z902) Ground circuit in the ACC harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z902) Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK RELATED HARNESS CONNECTIONS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all ACC harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections (if equipped).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the related component harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Reconnect all ACC harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Reconnect all in-line harness connectors (if equipped). Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Reconnect all related component harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace and program the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST. Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c2129-17 battery voltage - circuit voltage above threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C2129-17</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BATTERY VOLTAGE - CIRCUIT VOLTAGE ABOVE THRESHOLD</small><small>العطل: فولتية الدائرة أعلى من الحد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects that the voltage to the module is above 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RELATED DTC(S) PRESENT IN THE PCM</li><li>HIGH BATTERY VOLTAGE</li><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>RELATED DTCS PRESENT IN THE PCM</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the Engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Powertrain Control Module (PCM) DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any charging system or battery related DTCs present in the PCM?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the PCM DTC(s). Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC Module DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this Module. Wiggle the wiring and connectors while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check Service Bulletins for any possible causes that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c212a-84 system voltage - signal below allowable range\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C212A-84</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SYSTEM VOLTAGE - SIGNAL BELOW ALLOWABLE RANGE</small><small>العطل: الإشارة أقل من المدى المسموح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module receives a low charging system voltage message over the CAN Bus.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CHARGING SYSTEM VOLTAGE LOW</li><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK PCM FOR CHARGING SYSTEM DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Are there any charging system or battery DTCs set in the PCM?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the PCM DTC(s). Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK OTHER MODULES FOR CHARGING SYSTEM DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the Engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any other modules setting a charging system or battery related DTC?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">This is an indication of a charging/battery system malfunction. Check the battery/charging system in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to GR8 ELECTRICAL SYSTEM TESTER .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">If no other modules are reporting any charging system under voltage DTCs, replace and program the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this Module. Wiggle the wiring and connectors while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check Service Bulletins for any possible causes that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">No Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c212a-85 system voltage - signal above allowable range\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C212A-85</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SYSTEM VOLTAGE - SIGNAL ABOVE ALLOWABLE RANGE</small><small>العطل: الإشارة أعلى من المدى المسموح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode. ACC system is enabled and engaged.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module receives a high charging system voltage message over the Can Bus.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CHARGING SYSTEM VOLTAGE HIGH</li><li>RELATED DTC(S) PRESENT IN THE PCM</li><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK PCM FOR CHARGING SYSTEM DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any charging system or battery DTCs set in the PCM?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the PCM DTC(s). Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK OTHER MODULES</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Start the Engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Do any other modules display this type of DTC?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">This is an indication of a charging/battery system malfunction. Check the battery/charging system in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to GR8 ELECTRICAL SYSTEM TESTER .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC Module DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">If no other modules are reporting any charging system or over voltage DTCs, replace and program the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this Module. Wiggle the wiring and connectors while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check Service Bulletins for any possible causes that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c2206-00 vehicle configuration mismatch\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C2206-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">VEHICLE CONFIGURATION MISMATCH</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The vehicle configuration does not match what is stored in the ACC Module</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>VEHICLE CONFIGURATION</li><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL MODULE NOT PROPERLY CONFIGURED</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Preform the horizontal sensor alignment procedure in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does this DTC reset?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test Complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c2210-00 ecu overtemperature\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C2210-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ECU OVERTEMPERATURE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects an internal temperature greater than 115°C (239°F).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMBIENT TEMPERATURE TOO HIGH</li><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           To help in the service of the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) System, it is recommended speaking to the customer to find out what type of environment they were driving in when the cruise concern took place. Heavy rain, snow, ice, and fog can cause the ACC system to become unavailable. This is considered normal operation and no repair is necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC Module DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Make sure the lens is free of dirt, damage, and other obstructions and clean/repair as</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>VERIFY AMBIENT TEMPERATURE READING</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read PCM ambient air temperature.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the ambient air temperature reading 85°C (185°F) or above?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module has detected the ambient temperature above operating range. Once the temperature has decreased below 85°C (185°F), ACC operation will be restored.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace and program the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c2212-00 ecu in - plant mode active\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C2212-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ECU IN - PLANT MODE ACTIVE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Body Control Module (BCM) does not expect the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) module to be present.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) NOT CONFIGURED FOR ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL</li><li>(ACC) MODULE</li><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) MODULE NOT CONFIGURED</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL MODULE NOT PROGRAMED</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code will set if the Body Control Module (BCM) is not configured for Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Program the BCM.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Program the BCM with the correct sales code in accordance with the service information. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX . Verify that both the ACC Horizontal and Vertical alignments are correct. Perform the Adaptive Speed Control Module Alignment procedures. Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), MODULE PROGRAMMING .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c2225-00 pcm disabled ecu\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C2225-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">PCM DISABLED ECU</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects an active Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) is set in the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE DTC PRESENT</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will set if a DTC is detected in the Powertrain Control Module (PCM).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair the PCM DTC(s).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Repair the PCM DTC(s) in accordance with the service information. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c2226-00 tcm disabled ecu\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C2226-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">TCM DISABLED ECU</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode. ACC or Forward Collision Warning (FCW) system is enabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects an active Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) is set in the Transmission Control Module (TCM).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) DTC(S) PRESENT</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR TRANSMISSION CONTROL MODULE (TCM) DTCS</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will set if a DTC is detected in the Transmission Control Module (TCM).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair the TCM DTC(s).</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Repair the TCM DTC(s) in accordance with the service information. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c2227-00 abs disabled ecu\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C2227-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ABS DISABLED ECU</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects an active Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) is set in the Antilock Brake System (ABS) Module.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ANTILOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) MODULE DTC(S) PRESENT</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR ANTILOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) MODULE DTCS</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) will set if a DTC is detected in the Antilock Brake System (ABS) module.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Repair Diagnostic Trouble Code(s) set in the Antilock Brake System (ABS) module.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Repair Diagnostic Trouble Code(s) in the Antilock Brake System (ABS) module in accordance with the service information. Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"c2318-76 front camera - wrong mounting position\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">C2318-76</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">FRONT CAMERA - WRONG MOUNTING POSITION</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Speed Control Switch uses a Lin Bus to communicate to the Steering Column Control Module (SCCM). The SCCM then broadcast the speed control switch status over the Can Bus. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) module monitors the Can Bus for speed control switch status.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module has received over the Can Bus that the Speed Control Switch is functioning improperly.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>SPEED CONTROL SWITCH</li><li>STEERING WHEEL WIRING HARNESS / CONNECTORS</li><li>STEERING COLUMN CONTROL MODULE (SCCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC Module DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase ACC DTCs,</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC Module DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK SPEED CONTROL SWITCH OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Speed Control Switch status under the Steering Column Control Module (SCCM) while pressing multiple switch positions.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the switch positions change correctly in the scan tool?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">If any Body Control Module (BCM) Bus related DTCs are present, perform those respective diagnostic procedures first and recheck. Inspect the wiring and connectors between the SCCM and the Speed Control Switch and the output to the BCM for any possible problems. If no problems are found, replace and program the SCCM in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Inspect the wiring and connectors between the SCCM and the Speed Control Switch. If no problems are found, replace the Speed Control Switch in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SWITCH, SPEED CONTROL, REMOVAL .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this Module, Speed Control Switch and the Steering Column Control Module (SCCM). Wiggle the wiring and connectors while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check Service Bulletins for any possible causes that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1593-2a speed control switch 1/2 stuck\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1593-2A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SPEED CONTROL SWITCH 1/2 STUCK</small><small>العطل: عالق (Stuck)</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Speed Control Switch uses a Lin Bus to communicate to the Steering Column Control Module (SCCM). The SCCM then broadcast the speed control switch status over the Can Bus. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) module monitors the Can Bus for speed control switch status.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode. ACC is enabled and engaged.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module has received over the Can Bus that the Speed Control Switch is stuck in an on position.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>SPEED CONTROL SWITCH STUCK</li><li>STEERING WHEEL WIRING HARNESS / CONNECTORS</li><li>SPEED CONTROL SWITCH</li><li>STEERING COLUMN CONTROL MODULE (SCCM)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase ACC Module DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition off</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Activate the ACC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC Module DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK SPEED CONTROL SWITCH OPERATION</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Speed Control Switch status under the Steering Column Control Module (SCCM) while pressing multiple switch positions.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the switch positions change correctly in the scan tool?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">If any Body Control Module (BCM) Bus related DTCs are present, perform those respective diagnostic procedures first and recheck. Inspect the wiring and connectors between the SCCM and the Speed Control Switch and the output to the BCM for any possible problems. If no problems are found, replace and program the SCCM in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Inspect the wiring and connectors between the SCCM and the Speed Control Switch. If no problems are found, replace the Speed Control Switch in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SWITCH, SPEED CONTROL, REMOVAL .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this Module, Speed Control Switch and the Steering Column Control Module (SCCM). Wiggle the wiring and connectors while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">terminals, and correct pin tension.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check Service Bulletins for any possible causes that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Were there any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"p1666-00 cruise control module internal\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">P1666-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CRUISE CONTROL MODULE INTERNAL</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Module regularly performs internal controller diagnostic test and an internal hardware failure has been detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">VERIFY DTC IS ACTIVE</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using a scan tool, read ACC DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Is this DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Check for any controller updates. If no updates are available, erase DTC and cycle the ignition off then on. If the DTC resets, repeat erasing the DTC and cycling the ignition at least 3 times. If the DTC continues to reset, replace and program the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">No repair is necessary. Make sure the lens is free of dirt, damage, and other obstructions. Clear the DTC and verify the proper operation of the ACC system.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0002-00 can c bus off performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0002-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CAN C BUS OFF PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For an in-depth explanation of the Controller Area Network (CAN) system operation, refer to DESCRIPTION .</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition is on. Battery voltage is between 9.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CAN C bus has experienced a failure due to a circuit or processor fault.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>OPEN OR SHORTED CAN C BUS CIRCUIT</li><li>CAN C RELATED MODULE</li><li>CAN C RELATED STAR CONNECTOR (IF EQUIPPED)</li><li>CAN C RELATED SPLICE BLOCK CONNECTOR (IF EQUIPPED)</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:              If the scan tool will not communicate with CAN C, proceed to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C .</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, run a Vehicle Scan Report and attached it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the Vehicle Scan Report, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Proceed to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>ATTEMPT TO LOCATE AN INTERMITTENT CIRCUIT FAULT</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The scan tool LOSS OF COMM TEST will force the modules on the CAN C bus to continuously ping each other.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, initiate the LOSS OF COMM TEST.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A value above 0 under the NUMBER OF NO RESPONSES can help indicate the location of a circuit fault while wiggling the related CAN C bus circuits.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The scan tool lag time between pings is almost 1 full second. Keep this in mind while wiggling the wires and connectors.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>In a systematic manner, wiggle the applicable CAN C circuits at each related module, in-line connector, and Star/Splice Block Connector (if equipped) while monitoring the NUMBER OF NO RESPONSES on the scan tool.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the above test help locate the fault?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>PERFORM VISUAL INSPECTION OF CONNECTORS, TERMINALS AND WIRES</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all CAN C related module harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Inspect the harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Connect all CAN C related module harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Using the Vehicle Scan Report, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Proceed to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN C .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">The conditions that caused this DTC to set are no longer present. Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0009-00 high speed can communication bus (-) shorted to bus (+)\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0009-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">HIGH SPEED CAN COMMUNICATION BUS (-) SHORTED TO BUS (+)</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0100-00 lost communication with ecm/pcm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0100-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH ECM/PCM</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع ECM/PCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0101-00 lost communication with tcm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0101-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH TCM</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع TCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0102-00 lost communication with transfer case control module / awd\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0102-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH TRANSFER CASE CONTROL MODULE / AWD</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع TRANSFER CASE CONTROL MODULE / AWD</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0121-00 lost communication with anti-lock brake system (abs) control\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0121-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) CONTROL</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع ANTI-LOCK BRAKE SYSTEM (ABS) CONTROL</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">MODULE</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0132-00 lost communication with suspension control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0132-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH SUSPENSION CONTROL MODULE</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع SUSPENSION CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0140-00 lost communication with body control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0140-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH BODY CONTROL MODULE</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع BODY CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0151-00 lost communication with occupant restraint controller (orc)\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0151-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع OCCUPANT RESTRAINT CONTROLLER (ORC)</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0155-00 lost communication with cluster-ccn\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0155-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH CLUSTER-CCN</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع CLUSTER-CCN</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0293-00 lost communication with hybrid control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0293-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH HYBRID CONTROL MODULE</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع HYBRID CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0401-00 implausible data received from ecm/pcm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0401-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM ECM/PCM</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من ECM/PCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0402-00 implausible data received from tcm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0402-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM TCM</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من TCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0403-00 implausible data received from t-case\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0403-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM T-CASE</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من T-CASE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0415-00 implausible data received from abs\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0415-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM ABS</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من ABS</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0421-00 implausible data received from suspension control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0421-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM SUSPENSION CONTROL MODULE</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من SUSPENSION CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0422-00 implausible data received from body control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0422-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM BODY CONTROL MODULE</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من BODY CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0423-00 implausible data received from cluster-ccn\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0423-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM CLUSTER-CCN</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من CLUSTER-CCN</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0429-00 implausible data received from scm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0429-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM SCM</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من SCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0452-00 implausible data received from restraints control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0452-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM RESTRAINTS CONTROL MODULE</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من RESTRAINTS CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0594-00 implausible data received from hcp\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0594-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM HCP</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من HCP</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        This DTC indicates that the Hybrid Control Processor (HCP) is not sending a valid message over the Controller Area Network (CAN) bus. Therefore, the HCP is considered to be the &quot;offending module&quot;. The &quot;offending module&quot; will be</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">referred to in the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC procedure.</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1015-00 internal can a communication bus off\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1015-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">INTERNAL CAN A COMMUNICATION BUS OFF</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u110a-00 lost communication with scm - can-c\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U110A-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH SCM - CAN-C</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع SCM - CAN-C</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u11f9-00 engine did not respond to acc torque request\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U11F9-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ENGINE DID NOT RESPOND TO ACC TORQUE REQUEST</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode. ACC or Forward Collision Warning (FCW) system is enabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Module detects that the Powertrain Control Module is not responding to Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) module torque request.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM) DTCS PRESENT</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS PRESENT</li><li>POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) IMPROPERLY CONFIGURED</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR OTHER DTCS</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         To help in the service of the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system, it is recommended to communicate with the customer to obtain the environmental conditions they were driving in when the cruise control concern took place. Heavy rain, snow, ice, and fog can cause the ACC system to become inoperative. This is considered as a normal operational reaction of the ACC system and no repair is necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>This is an informational Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC). The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module communicates over the CAN Bus with the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) to increase engine speed when needed. If other ACC Module DTCs are present, perform their respective diagnostic procedures first.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Check for:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">PCM DTCs present. PCM improperly configured. BCM DTCs present. BCM improperly configured. Implausible DTCs against the PCM. Any Service Bulletins that may apply.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Were any of the above conditions present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Refer to the appropriate diagnostic procedure repair/reprogram as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Erase this DTC and Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST. If the DTC continues to set, no other modules are reporting any DTCs, and all modules are configured properly, replace and program the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1215-00 lost communication with forward facing camera\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1215-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH FORWARD FACING CAMERA</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع FORWARD FACING CAMERA</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Continuously with the engine running. System voltage between 10.0 and 16.0 volts. No CAN Bus off or shorted DTCs present. Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module is not in Plant-Mode. ESP is not in diagnostic mode. ACC and the Forward Collision Warning (FCW) systems are both enabled.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) module communicates with the Forward Facing Camera (FFC) on a dedicated Can C Bus. This DTC will set when the ACC Module is unable to communicate with the FFC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will have limited functionality. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>FUSED IGNITION (RUN) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>CAN C BUS (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>CAN C BUS (-)CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>CAN C BUS (+) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>CAN C BUS (-) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>CAN C BUS (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO CAN C BUS (+) CIRCUIT</li><li>FORWARD FACING CAMERA</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) DTCs Module DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase ACC Module DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC Module DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 9</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE (F924) FUSED IGNITION (RUN) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Forward Facing Camera Module (FFCM) harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the Engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F924) Fused Ignition (Run) circuit at the FFCM harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F924) Fused Ignition (Run) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the fuse is open, make sure to check for a short to ground.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (Z911) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check the (Z911) Ground circuit at the FFCM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z911) Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D449) CAN C(+) AND (D448) CAN C(-) CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the and both (D449) CAN C (+) and (D448) CAN C(-) circuits at the FFCM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and either the (D449) CAN C (+) or the (D448) CAN C(-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D449) CAN C (+) and/or the (D448) CAN C(-) circuit(s) for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 5</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>CHECK THE (D449) CAN C(+) AND D448 CAN C(-) CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of both (D449) CAN C (+) and (D448) CAN C(-) circuits between the ACC Module harness connector and the FFCM harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 1.0 Ohm on both circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 6</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D449) CAN C (+) and/or the (D448) CAN C(-) circuit(s) for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>CHECK THE (D449) CAN C(+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO THE D448 CAN C(-) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the continuity between the (D449) CAN C (+) and (D448) CAN C(-) circuit at the ACC Module harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (D449) CAN C (+) and (D448) CAN C(-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D449) CAN C (+) circuit for a short to the (D448) CAN C(-) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 7</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>CHECK THE (D449) CAN C(+) AND D448 CAN C(-) CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TO VOLTAGE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the voltage of both the (D449) CAN C (+) and (D448) CAN C(-) circuits at the ACC Module harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D449) CAN C (+) and/or the (D448) CAN C(-) circuit(s) for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 8</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>FORWARD FACING CAMERA</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace and program/align the Forward Facing Camera Module (FFCM) in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, FORWARD FACING CAMERA (FFCM), REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">If this DTC resets after replacement of the Forward Facing Camera and no other problems are found, replace and program the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), REMOVAL .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test Complete.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>CHECK THE WIRING AND CONNECTORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>The conditions necessary to set the DTC are not present at this time.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Using the schematics as a guide, inspect the wiring and connectors specific to this Module. Wiggle the wiring and connectors while checking for shorted and open circuits.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Check Service Bulletins for any possible causes that may apply.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Were any problems found?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACC) VERIFICATION TEST.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u121e-00 lost communication with steering wheel cruise control switch\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U121E-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH STEERING WHEEL CRUISE CONTROL SWITCH</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع STEERING WHEEL CRUISE CONTROL SWITCH</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">IF the Body Control Module (BCM), Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) module, or Steering Column Control Module (SCCM) has any other lost communication DTCs present, perform those respective test first. If no other communication DTCs are set, refer to the SCCM diagnostics and perform the diagnostic procedure for U121E- 00-Lost Communication With Steering Wheel Cruise Control Switch as if the DTC is active.</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u141e-00 implausible data received from cruise control switch\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U141E-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM CRUISE CONTROL SWITCH</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من CRUISE CONTROL SWITCH</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u148d-00 implausible data received from forward facing camera\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U148D-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">IMPLAUSIBLE DATA RECEIVED FROM FORWARD FACING CAMERA</small><small>بيانات غير منطقية مستلمة من FORWARD FACING CAMERA</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1600-00 ecu application software mismatch\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1600-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">ECU APPLICATION SOFTWARE MISMATCH</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">One time during an ignition cycle.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) Module was reprogrammed with a corrupted flash file, or the reprogramming of the ACC was interrupted before it was complete.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display &quot;ACC/FCW Unavailable Service Required&quot;. The Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) system will be disabled. Once the DTC changes from active to stored, the ACC feature will return to normal operation. The DTC will be cleared after a 100 consecutive ignition cycles with no active detection.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL MODULE NOT PROGRAMMED PROPERLY</li><li>ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL MODULE</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">ACC Verification Test</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all jumper wires and reconnect all previously disconnected components and connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Make sure that all accessories are turned off and that the battery is fully charged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If the ACC Module was replaced or moved in any way, the ACC Module must be aligned. Perform both the Vertical and Horizontal Sensor Alignment procedures in accordance with the Service Information.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Refer to MODULE, ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL (ACCM), MODULE PROGRAMMING .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Test drive the vehicle and verify proper operation.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read ACC Module DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are there any DTCs present in the ACC Module?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the ACC Module DTC(s). Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Article GUID: A00910358</p></div></div></details></div></details></div>";
